$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">The number of acres of useful timberland in 13&nbsp;counties in California is summarized in the box plot above. Which of the following is closest to the median number of acres?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">4,399</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">7,067</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">8,831</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">10,595</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is correct. The median of the data summarized by a box plot is the value associated with the vertical line segment within the box. According to the box plot shown, this value is slightly greater than 7,000. Therefore, the closest value for the median number of acres is 7,067.<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the value associated with the vertical line segment forming the left-hand side of the box. Choice C is incorrect. This value is greater than the value associated with the vertical line segment within the box. Choice D is incorrect. This is the value associated with the vertical line segment forming the right-hand side of the box.</p></p>
$SATQ$, false, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$Multiple Choice$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"374b18f9","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"028959-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.C.","skill_desc":"One-variable data: Distributions and measures of center and spread","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":1,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \">\n        <div class=\"standalone_image \">\n          <img src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/374b18f9/img_000_488f6dec.png\" alt=\"The figure presents a box plot titled &ldquo;Acres of useful timberland.&rdquo; The numbers 1,000 through 14,000, in increments of 1,000, are indicated on the horizontal axis. The data represented by the box plot are as follows. Note that all values are approximate. In the box plot, the left whisker extends from 1,100 to 4,500; the box extends from 4,500 to 10,500; a vertical line segment at 7,100 divides the box into 2 parts; and the right whisker extends from 10,500 to 13,300.\" width=\"215\" height=\"71\">\n        </div>\n      </div>\n","stem":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">The number of acres of useful timberland in 13&nbsp;counties in California is summarized in the box plot above. Which of the following is closest to the median number of acres?</p>\n","answerOptions":[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">4,399</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">7,067</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">8,831</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">10,595</p>\n"}],"keys":null,"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. The median of the data summarized by a box plot is the value associated with the vertical line segment within the box. According to the box plot shown, this value is slightly greater than 7,000. Therefore, the closest value for the median number of acres is 7,067.<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the value associated with the vertical line segment forming the left-hand side of the box. Choice C is incorrect. This value is greater than the value associated with the vertical line segment within the box. Choice D is incorrect. This is the value associated with the vertical line segment forming the right-hand side of the box.</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":1,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959623,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"374b18f9","skill_cd":"Q.C.","score_band_range_cd":1,"skill_desc":"One-variable data: Distributions and measures of center and spread","createDate":1691007959623,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":"028959-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"Q","uId":"785961e4-5a9d-4dea-ba48-c0911fd63426","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"028959-DC","section":"Math","body":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \">\n        <div class=\"standalone_image \">\n          <img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"The figure presents a box plot titled &ldquo;Acres of useful timberland.&rdquo; The numbers 1,000 through 14,000, in increments of 1,000, are indicated on the horizontal axis. The data represented by the box plot are as follows. Note that all values are approximate. In the box plot, the left whisker extends from 1,100 to 4,500; the box extends from 4,500 to 10,500; a vertical line segment at 7,100 divides the box into 2 parts; and the right whisker extends from 10,500 to 13,300.\" width=\"215\" height=\"71\">\n        </div>\n      </div>\n","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">The number of acres of useful timberland in 13&nbsp;counties in California is summarized in the box plot above. Which of the following is closest to the median number of acres?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">4,399</p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">7,067</p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">8,831</p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">10,595</p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"b","rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. The median of the data summarized by a box plot is the value associated with the vertical line segment within the box. According to the box plot shown, this value is slightly greater than 7,000. Therefore, the closest value for the median number of acres is 7,067.<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the value associated with the vertical line segment forming the left-hand side of the box. Choice C is incorrect. This value is greater than the value associated with the vertical line segment within the box. Choice D is incorrect. This is the value associated with the vertical line segment forming the right-hand side of the box.</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959623,"updateDate":1691007959623}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959623, 1691007959623),
    ($SATQ$37930b2a$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$028921-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.G.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Evaluating statistical claims: Observational studies and experiments $SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">Residents of a town were surveyed to determine whether they are satisfied with the concession stand&nbsp;at the local park. A random sample of 200&nbsp;residents was selected. All 200 responded, and&nbsp;87% said they are satisfied. Based on this information, which of the following statements must&nbsp;be true?<p class="list_paragraph ">I. Of all the town residents, 87% would say they are satisfied with the concession stand at the local park.<br>
II. If another random sample of 200&nbsp;residents were surveyed, 87% would&nbsp;say they are satisfied.</p></p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">Neither</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">I only</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">II only</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">I and II</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is correct. The purpose of surveying a random sample of residents is to approximate the percent of the town residents that are satisfied with the concession stand. The sample doesn&rsquo;t necessarily get the same result as surveying every resident of the town, nor would another sample necessarily have identical results. Therefore, although it&rsquo;s possible that either statement I or statement II could prove true by surveying every resident of the town, these statements cannot be proven true solely based on the results of the sample.<p>Choice B is incorrect because surveying a sample of the town residents may not have the same result as surveying all the town residents. Choices C and D are incorrect because surveying a different sample of residents could yield different results.</p></p>
