n"}],"keys":null,"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. If 1,200 customers register for new accounts every day, then (1,200)(5) = 6,000 customers registered for new accounts in the first 5 days. Therefore, of the first 60,000 new accounts that were registered, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/38a9ac45/img_004_3d3be6ce.png\" alt=\"the fraction 6,000 over 60,000\"></span>, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/38a9ac45/img_005_e169c1e3.png\" alt=\"the fraction 1 over 10\"></span>, were registered in the first 5 days.<p>Choice A is incorrect. The fraction&nbsp;<span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/38a9ac45/img_006_5dba61cf.png\" alt=\"one fifth \"></span> represents the fraction of accounts registered in 1 of the first 5 days. Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or computation errors. Choice D is incorrect. The fraction&nbsp;<span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/38a9ac45/img_007_838f996f.png\" alt=\"1 over 50\"></span> represents the fraction of the first 60,000 accounts that were registered in 1 day.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":8,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959634,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"38a9ac45","skill_cd":"Q.E.","score_band_range_cd":4,"skill_desc":"Probability and conditional probability","createDate":1691007959634,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":"07853-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"Q","uId":"9e29fd58-b175-46a0-93ab-00e3bfd5f589","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"07853-DC","section":"Math","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">If 1,200 customers register for new accounts at a social media website every day, what fraction of the first 60,000 new accounts are registered in the first 5 days?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"one fifth\"></span></span></p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"one tenth\"></span></span></p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"one twelfth\"></span></span></p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"1 over 50\"></span></span></p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"b","rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. If 1,200 customers register for new accounts every day, then (1,200)(5) = 6,000 customers registered for new accounts in the first 5 days. Therefore, of the first 60,000 new accounts that were registered, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the fraction 6,000 over 60,000\"></span>, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the fraction 1 over 10\"></span>, were registered in the first 5 days.<p>Choice A is incorrect. The fraction&nbsp;<span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"one fifth \"></span> represents the fraction of accounts registered in 1 of the first 5 days. Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or computation errors. Choice D is incorrect. The fraction&nbsp;<span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"1 over 50\"></span> represents the fraction of the first 60,000 accounts that were registered in 1 day.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959634,"updateDate":1691007959634}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959634, 1691007959634),
    ($SATQ$391ae4b2$SATQ$, $SATQ$4135b77c-4178-4cdc-8f4a-8f46e634b934$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$bcc03d51-28b8-4cb4-b581-0dd6e426b575$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$One-variable data: Distributions and measures of center and spread$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Data set F consists of <math alttext="55"><mn>55</mn>
</math> integers between <math alttext="170"><mn>170</mn>
</math> and <math alttext="290"><mn>290</mn>
</math>. Data set G consists of all the integers in data set F as well as the integer <math alttext="10"><mn>10</mn>
</math>. Which of the following must be less for data set F than for data set G?</p>
<ol style="list-style-type: upper-roman;">
<li style="text-align: left;">The mean</li>
<li style="text-align: left;">The median</li>
</ol>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"1694d33e-d682-4de8-a116-a0ef880c9e66","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">I only</p>"},{"id":"84d8c6af-88b5-42f9-9555-1ec0e8605d3a","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">II only</p>"},{"id":"ef1c7321-f4ad-4733-8951-96990e111b43","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">I and II</p>"},{"id":"46c11864-c95d-46b1-ac26-b6ec4faf05ed","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Neither I nor II</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["46c11864-c95d-46b1-ac26-b6ec4faf05ed"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is correct. It's given that data set F consists of <math alttext="55"><mn>55</mn>
</math> integers between <math alttext="170"><mn>170</mn>
</math> and <math alttext="290"><mn>290</mn>
</math> and data set G consists of all the integers in data set F as well as the integer <math alttext="10"><mn>10</mn>
</math>. Since the integer <math alttext="10"><mn>10</mn>
</math> is less than all the integers in data set F, the mean of data set G must be less than the mean of data set F. Thus, the mean of data set F isn't less than the mean of data set G. When a data set is in ascending order, the median is between the two middle values when there is an even number of values and the median is the middle value when there is an odd number of values. It follows that the median of data set F is either greater than or equal to the median of data set G. Therefore, the median of data set F isn't less than the median of data set G. Thus, neither the mean nor the median must be less for data set F than for data set G.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"391ae4b2","external_id":"4135b77c-4178-4cdc-8f4a-8f46e634b934","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"bcc03d51-28b8-4cb4-b581-0dd6e426b575","uId":"b8fe154b-37b8-4187-863c-dd1005243c95","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.C.","skill_desc":"One-variable data: Distributions and measures of center and spread","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Data set F consists of <math alttext=\"55\"><mn>55</mn>\n</math> integers between <math alttext=\"170\"><mn>170</mn>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"290\"><mn>290</mn>\n</math>. Data set G consists of all the integers in data set F as well as the integer <math alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn>\n</math>. Which of the following must be less for data set F than for data set G?</p>\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-roman;\">\n<li style=\"text-align: left;\">The mean</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: left;\">The median</li>\n</ol>","answerOptions":[{"id":"1694d33e-d682-4de8-a116-a0ef880c9e66","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">I only</p>"},{"id":"84d8c6af-88b5-42f9-9555-1ec0e8605d3a","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">II only</p>"},{"id":"ef1c7321-f4ad-4733-8951-96990e111b43","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">I and II</p>"},{"id":"46c11864-c95d-46b1-ac26-b6ec4faf05ed","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Neither I nor II</p>"}],"keys":["46c11864-c95d-46b1-ac26-b6ec4faf05ed"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. It's given that data set F consists of <math alttext=\"55\"><mn>55</mn>\n</math> integers between <math alttext=\"170\"><mn>170</mn>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"290\"><mn