rOptions":[{"id":"99d42a7f-c760-4a89-8cca-cbb17b377c70","content":"<p><math alttext=\"8 percent sign\"><mn>8</mn>\n<mo>%</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"f2da3df8-54e3-4b7e-beab-ff60c46de504","content":"<p><math alttext=\"36 percent sign\"><mn>36</mn>\n<mo>%</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"ad3ded08-4c68-4eac-b783-54377feaa14f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"72 percent sign\"><mn>72</mn>\n<mo>%</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"bbef6efe-bdfb-45a5-bd31-898e0f21a559","content":"<p><math alttext=\"92 percent sign\"><mn>92</mn>\n<mo>%</mo></math></p>"}],"correct_answer":["D"]},"createDate":1691007959831,"updateDate":1691007959831}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959831, 1691007959831),
    ($SATQ$3ac09984$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$10654-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">Marta has 7,500 pesos she will convert to US&nbsp;dollars using a currency exchange service. At this time, the currency exchange rate is 1 peso = 0.075 US dollars. The exchange service will charge Marta a 2% fee on the converted US dollar amount. How many US dollars will Marta receive from the currency exchange after the 2% fee is applied?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p><span class=\"align align-52\">$551.25</span></p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p><span class=\"align align-52\">$562.50</span></p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p><span class=\"align align-52\">$5,625.00</span></p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p><span class=\"align align-52\">$98,000.00</span></p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is correct. At the exchange rate of 1 peso = 0.075 US dollars, 7,500 pesos would be converted to 7,500 &times; 0.075 = $562.50. However, since Maria pays a 2% fee on the converted US dollar amount, she receives only (100 &ndash; 2)%, or 98%, of the converted US dollars, and 562.50 &times; 0.98 = $551.25.<p>Choice B is incorrect. This is the number of US dollars Maria would receive if the exchange service did not charge a 2% fee. Choice C is incorrect and may result from a decimal point error made when calculating the conversion to US dollars and from not assessing the 2% fee. Choice D is incorrect and may result from reversing the units of the exchange rate.</p></p>
$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$Multiple Choice$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"3ac09984","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"10654-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.A.","skill_desc":"Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">Marta has 7,500 pesos she will convert to US&nbsp;dollars using a currency exchange service. At this time, the currency exchange rate is 1 peso = 0.075 US dollars. The exchange service will charge Marta a 2% fee on the converted US dollar amount. How many US dollars will Marta receive from the currency exchange after the 2% fee is applied?</p>\n","answerOptions":[{"id":"a","content":"<p><span class=\"align align-52\">$551.25</span></p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p><span class=\"align align-52\">$562.50</span></p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p><span class=\"align align-52\">$5,625.00</span></p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p><span class=\"align align-52\">$98,000.00</span></p>\n"}],"keys":null,"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is correct. At the exchange rate of 1 peso = 0.075 US dollars, 7,500 pesos would be converted to 7,500 &times; 0.075 = $562.50. However, since Maria pays a 2% fee on the converted US dollar amount, she receives only (100 &ndash; 2)%, or 98%, of the converted US dollars, and 562.50 &times; 0.98 = $551.25.<p>Choice B is incorrect. This is the number of US dollars Maria would receive if the exchange service did not charge a 2% fee. Choice C is incorrect and may result from a decimal point error made when calculating the conversion to US dollars and from not assessing the 2% fee. Choice D is incorrect and may result from reversing the units of the exchange rate.</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959638,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"3ac09984","skill_cd":"Q.A.","score_band_range_cd":3,"skill_desc":"Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units","createDate":1691007959638,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":"10654-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"Q","uId":"948bda31-761c-470a-9992-67f6c9d3afad","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"10654-DC","section":"Math","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">Marta has 7,500 pesos she will convert to US&nbsp;dollars using a currency exchange service. At this time, the currency exchange rate is 1 peso = 0.075 US dollars. The exchange service will charge Marta a 2% fee on the converted US dollar amount. How many US dollars will Marta receive from the currency exchange after the 2% fee is applied?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p><span class=\"align align-52\">$551.25</span></p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p><span class=\"align align-52\">$562.50</span></p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p><span class=\"align align-52\">$5,625.00</span></p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p><span class=\"align align-52\">$98,000.00</span></p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"a","rationale":"<p>Choice A is correct. At the exchange rate of 1 peso = 0.075 US dollars, 7,500 pesos would be converted to 7,500 &times; 0.075 = $562.50. However, since Maria pays a 2% fee on the converted US dollar amount, she receives only (100 &ndash; 2)%, or 98%, of the converted US dollars, and 562.50 &times; 0.98 = $551.25.<p>Choice B is incorrect. This is the number of US dollars Maria would receive if the exchange service did not charge a 2% fee. Choice C is incorrect and may result from a decimal point error made when calculating the conversion to US dollars and from not assessing the 2% fee. Choice D is incorrect and may result from reversing the units of the exchange rate.</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959638,"updateDate":1691007959638}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959638