$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/445dd032/img_000_97f3946f.png\" alt=\"3 times, open parenthesis, 13 point 5 0 z, close parenthesis \"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/445dd032/img_001_ab0f7f73.png\" alt=\"3 plus 13 point 5 0 z\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/445dd032/img_002_cfacdeea.png\" alt=\"3 z plus 13 point 5 0 z\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/445dd032/img_003_5c5ca7c4.png\" alt=\"13 point 5 0 times, open parenthesis, z plus 3, close parenthesis\"></span></span></p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is correct. It&rsquo;s given that when Tanya works <span class="italic">z</span> hours, she earns <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/445dd032/img_006_e3a06f16.png" alt="13 point 5 0 z"></span> dollars. Since her hourly rate is constant, if she works 3 times as many hours, or <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/445dd032/img_007_ae334d78.png" alt="3 z"></span> hours, she will earn 3 times as many dollars, or <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/445dd032/img_008_2ea8b3e8.png" alt="3 times, open parenthesis, 13 point 5 0 z, close parenthesis"></span>.<p>Choice B is incorrect. This expression represents adding 3 dollars to the <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/445dd032/img_009_e3a06f16.png" alt="13 point 5 0 z"></span> dollars Tanya will earn. Choice C is incorrect. This expression can be rewritten as <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/445dd032/img_010_06a5498c.png" alt="16 point 5 0 z"></span>, which implies that Tanya earns $16.50 per hour, not $13.50. Choice D is incorrect. This expression adds 3 to the number of hours Tanya works, rather than multiplying the hours she works by 3.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
